cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "RCM Path: a computed address layer for PostgreSQL (RCM Address Engine, experiments A2-A8)"
authors:
  - name: "Abu"
    alias: "tymakbayev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tymakbayev/RCM_Path"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-11-27
keywords:
  - PostgreSQL
  - index
  - minimal perfect hashing
  - hash-based addressing
  - LSM
  - sidecar
abstract: >-
  A sidecar address layer that computes the heap page of a PostgreSQL row from its key (minimal perfect hash cascade,
  8-bit fingerprint, page number; about 3-5 bytes per key instead of a ~31-byte B-tree), with the frozen protocols,
  code, raw results and reports of experiments A2-A8 on 1 and 10 million rows.
